# terafox, to match Neovim's colorscheme (init.lua sets nightfox.nvim's
# terafox variant). The theme file at themes/terafox.tmTheme was generated by
# nightfox's `bat` extra, so the two stay in step by construction.
#
# bat names custom themes after the filename, not the <key>name</key> inside
# the plist -- which nightfox hardcodes to "Catppuccin Macchiato" upstream in
# every theme it emits. Ignore it; the colours are terafox's.
#
# themes/ is only read when it has been compiled into the binary cache. After
# editing the .tmTheme, or after a `brew upgrade bat` resets the cache:
#
#     bat cache --build
--theme="terafox"
